{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458523-ancestors-and-mnesis-what-do-they-have-in-common-what-are-the-differences","id":1458523,"title":"Ancestors and Mnesis - what do they have in common, what are the differences?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-03T08:19:18-07:00","id":1458523,"title":"Ancestors and Mnesis - what do they have in common, what are the differences?","content":"What says in the title - trying to get a better hang of what each background does, in fluff and mechanically, to understand the conceptual space of either or both.<br /> <br /> Pardon the ignorance, it has been decades since i last played WtA, only with Garou and the background was called &quot;Past Lives&quot; back then, so lots of headspace to cover indeed.<br /> <br /> Trying to make sense of things to maybe hack &amp; tinker for a homebrew game of my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T11:24:56-07:00","id":1458548,"title":"","content":"Ancestors simply puts the character in communion with one of their ancestors so they can gain additional dice in an Ability. Do you need more Stealth? Roll your Ancestors rank against difficulty 8, and however many successes you have is an additional die per scene (once per game session). At an ST's discretion, you can roll at higher difficulty to receive either useful advice or precognitive visions. Presumably because you make contact with actual Ancestor spirits, you can then separately summon them and do everything else you normally would with a spirit.<br /> <br /> Mnesis is different. It is the racial memory of the specific Mokole stream (the Mokole grouped in a common geographic area - Australia, India, East Asia, and Africa/Americas - presumably combined because South America and Africa were once joined). You don't get ability dots with that. You only get the memory or impressions of what a specific ancestor has seen or done. There's an entire section in the Mokole tribebook on what information can't be gained, the hazards, and other complicating factors in the &quot;Mnesis quest.&quot; How far back in time you can do depends on the dots you put into the Background. To be honest, I think the practical value is limited. It's mainly an ST plot device.<br /> <br /> But there is also a Knowledge skill called Mnesis Emulation. You toll that + your Mnesis background traits against Difficulty 7. For every two successes (round up_, you get one additional trait in an Ability for one day. So if you get 5 successes, that gives you a 3. You can get a 3 dice in one skill for one day, or 1 dice in one skill for three days. The character needs to go into an overnight trance, so it's something not done on the spot, but prepared ahead of time. So that is a more complicated version of Ancestors.<br /> <br /> That seems to be how it is in 2e. Not sure if W20 handles it differently.<br /> <br /> As a concept &quot;mnesis&quot; is different than Ancestor spirits, so while they are similar in some results they are very different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T11:38:54-07:00","id":1458550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458523-ancestors-and-mnesis-what-do-they-have-in-common-what-are-the-differences?p=1458548#post1458548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (the Mokole grouped in a common geographic area - Australia, India, East Asia, and Africa/Americas - presumably combined because South America and Africa were once joined).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the Atlantic slave trade, which would've brought Mokole Kinfolk to the Americas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T12:30:08-07:00","id":1458559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458523-ancestors-and-mnesis-what-do-they-have-in-common-what-are-the-differences?p=1458550#post1458550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the Atlantic slave trade, which would've brought Mokole Kinfolk to the Americas.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the Atlantic slave trade didn't happen until 500 years ago. You have 10,000 years or more history before that happens. And crocodiles are native to the Americas in the Caribbean. Unless we think there were no Mokole at all before the Atlantic slave trade, you need to explain why Mokole in the Western Hemisphere are part of the same Stream as African Mokole despite there being no connection between the two. (I am assuming that is the case as opposed to there simply NOT being Mokole in the Americas until the African slave trade. I'm sure someone will correct me if I am wrong.)<br /> <br /> There's a difference between explaining why African Stream Mokole are in the Americas and why American and African Mokole are both part of the same stream. The most likely answer to me is that they have a common ancestor dating back to the time when the continents were joined, and that was important to Gaia for some reason.<br /> <br /> I know limited information on the Mokole so it's possible I am missing some explanations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T15:28:52-07:00","id":1458576,"title":"","content":"Oh well, still a little uncertain of which one would roll better with a Bene Gesserit-style &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bene_Gesserit#Other_Memory\" target=\"_blank\">blood memory</a>&quot; of sorts or how broken might it be to use bitts from both backgrounds to tailor what i'm looking for. Might end up hitting the PDFs anyway later on, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T16:29:54-07:00","id":1458581,"title":"","content":"Concept and description-wise:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ancestors</u></b> is a Garou's connection to their Ancestor Spirits. When they use this, they're communing with spirits and then receiving impressions from the lives of those spirits. This can be experienced in whatever way you think a spirit communion is experienced, it may be a dream-like trance, a voice in your head, or a Matrix-Style &quot;I just know&quot;. But whatever the case, it is limited to a spirit's ability and disposition to help.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mnesis</u></b> is the Mokol\u00e9's connection with their Collective Mind, so to speak. It is a kind of collective mental library that holds memories both of your past lives and of the lives of your brethren. They are the Memory of Gaia, so their main role in the world should be to commit things to memory, and then commit them to Mnesis. When you use Mnesis what you do is to travel through those accumulated memories, half experiencing the ones you're just brushing through, then fully experiencing the memory you want. Fully means fully, you relive that memory as if it was with yourself right now. No matter how long ago it was, t will be a fresh memory for you.<br /> <br /> In theory that's why the Mokol\u00e9 have such a resentment for the Garou. To them the war isn't just something in the past that happened to their ancestors and explains their current lot in life. Instead it is a set of very vivid and painful memories they relived when they searched the library for the topic &quot;Garou&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}